# Accepted container-scan findings for the backend image.
#
# The container scan runs at CRITICAL only (see .github/workflows/ci.yml). The
# dependency-audit gate (scripts/check-audit.mjs) already enforces HIGH at the
# npm-dependency level, so the container scan's job is to catch critical issues
# in the built image (incl. OS packages) that npm audit cannot see.

# CVE-2026-59873 — CRITICAL, DoS via crafted gzip bomb in `tar`.
# This lives in /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm (the npm CLI bundled into the
# node:22-alpine base image), NOT in our application dependencies or runtime
# path. The API never invokes the npm CLI or extracts untrusted tarballs at
# runtime, so it is unreachable. No fix is available in the current
# node:22-alpine tag (ships tar 7.5.11 < fixed 7.5.19). Revisit when the base
# image ships npm with tar >= 7.5.19.
CVE-2026-59873

# multer advisories — accepted at the dependency-audit gate (scripts/check-audit.mjs).
# No upload routes exist in Phase 0, so the parser is never invoked. Listed here so
# a future switch to a HIGH+CRITICAL container scan stays consistent with that gate.
GHSA-wc9g-mqfw-jrwm
GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf
